The network's header client is told the request headers as sent.

Network.requestWillBeSentExtraInfo shows what a request really carried, with what
the network adds after OnBeforeSendHeaders: Authorization, Proxy-Authorization, Host,
Connection. TrustedHeaderClient stops at OnBeforeSendHeaders, so a client sees the
Cookie but none of these. It gets a new message from the callback on the URLRequest that
already feeds DevToolsObserver.OnRawRequest, once for each transaction, with no change
to what is sent. DevTools' interceptor, which stands in the chain, passes it on.

Implementers of TrustedHeaderClient under chrome/ and in unit tests are not built here
and are not changed.

